  "excluded_from_partial_source": "Other projects, historical evidence, shipped synthetic sample_data and GitHub workflow files are not copied. The complete Freight runtime, maintained tests, browser sources and local guides are exact current blobs. Tests must use their own generated fixtures.",
  "claim_body": "## Demonstrated product defect\n\nOwner: `chatgpt:/root/migration_execution` (estate713adaab), under the continuing isolated-source contribution mandate.\n\nAn actual native Python 3.13.7 CLI run on synthetic Freight inputs places invoice CAL-7122 / load LD261054 on HOLD because its `pod_received` cell is N. Appending a second column with the same header and Y in that row leaves the original N cell present, but the existing CSV mapping silently selects Y. A second actual CLI run still exits zero, removes MISSING_POD, and changes that settlement to READY with net 260300 cents. No payment or real customer data is involved.\n\nThe two product processes return **0 / 0**. All source files and both input maps remain unchanged during execution. Raw commands, stdout/stderr, complete summaries and unchanged-state maps are retained natively at `/Users/me/Developer/workflow-checks-csv-header-713adaab/before-evidence/`. Report SHA256: `c40d85227e15f9eb0fa581237ae831fa9f883587b31312fd2d07d5c7047dee8c`.\n\nThe before-witness uses the existing qualified native partial packet-filename source, explicitly labelled in the receipt. Its discovery target `freight_packets/freightpkt/ingest.py` is unchanged Git blob `dad18f470035318241a9c432326d1f4bafa26edf`. Fresh full main `76e6175d91320ac816cee019df969c0f0e1bbfc7`, tree `256483cd5c7cbb3731e5a6c322a117900ab24b65`, retains that exact blob.\n\n## Exact implementation fence\n\n- `freight_packets/freightpkt/ingest.py`: admit unambiguous column names before its four CSV readers create row mappings.\n- New `freight_packets/tests/test_csv_header_admission.py`.\n- New `freight_packets/CSV_HEADERS.md`.\n- Unique `docs/verification/freight-csv-headers-713adaab/` evidence.\n\nReject repeated literal names for fixed-schema load/invoice CSVs. For the geofence and tracking CSVs, apply only their existing strip/lower header comparison when detecting repeats. Preserve distinct alias priority, ordinary extra columns, field/value parsing, timestamp and monetary behavior, invoice grouping, settlement logic and ordinary output bytes. The existing input loader must refuse before a malformed export replaces prior report artifacts.\n\nThis is bounded to those four existing ingest entrypoints. Ancillary fines/document/dispute loaders, JSON input, CLI, pipeline, review, web/UI, batch handoff, shared CI, and installed routes stay unchanged.\n\n## Ownership and qualification\n\nThe complete current 48-record project history, current central coordination updates and exact ingest history show no competing Freight column-admission scope. Utility PR24 retains its separate implementation. Freight #39/PR49 retains the already-qualified filename work; #50 retains saved-review comparison, and the completed #37 batch source is preserved.\n\nThe ThinkPad native coordination route remains unavailable after the recorded timeouts. Its inaccessible Conscience state is not treated as evidence of no owner and no native lease is asserted. The isolated Mac claim and provenance will be retained in Git alongside this public scope.\n\nQualify the actual failed/accepted CLI behavior, unchanged previous outputs on refusal, ordinary valid inputs, all four duplicate-header entrypoints, and the original header-normalization/alias contracts. Obtain independent source and raw-receipt review before normal exact-head integration. No service, installation, customer input, firmware or migration/cutover operation is included.\n"
